---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const title = "Pikos guides";
const description = "Walkthroughs for connecting a calendar and moving your notes and tasks into Pikos.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-8 py-20">

    <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-neutral-400 transition-colors hover:text-primary-500 dark:text-neutral-500 dark:hover:text-primary-400">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"/></svg>
      Home
    </a>

    <h1 class="mt-8 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50">Guides</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400">
      Most of Pikos needs no explaining. Two things do, because they reach outside the app: your calendar, and whatever you're moving away from.
    </p>

    <!-- Calendar sync -->
    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50">Connect a calendar</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300">
        Works with iCloud, Google Calendar, and any standard CalDAV server. Your events arrive as real pages, so the notes you take in a meeting live on the meeting.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300">
        The guide walks through app passwords and server URLs, then what a synced event does once it's in. Your password goes to the system keychain, not to a file Pikos owns.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
        <a href="/calendar-sync" class="font-medium text-primary-500 hover:underline dark:text-primary-400">Set up calendar sync &rarr;</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Import -->
    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50">Move in from another app</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300">
        Point Pikos at a folder of Markdown or a CSV export and it reads the structure rather than dumping the text. Obsidian, TickTick and Todoist each have a walkthrough of their own.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300">
        Exporting from something else? If it writes CSV, you map the columns once in a side-by-side preview and import.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
        <a href="/import" class="font-medium text-primary-500 hover:underline dark:text-primary-400">Import walkthroughs &rarr;</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div class="mt-16 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50 px-6 py-6 dark:border-neutral-800 dark:bg-neutral-900">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50">Stuck on something that isn't here?</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300">
        The <a href="/faq" class="font-medium text-primary-500 hover:underline dark:text-primary-400">FAQ</a> covers the questions that come up most. Anything else, <a href="/feedback" class="font-medium text-primary-500 hover:underline dark:text-primary-400">tell me</a> and I'll write the guide.
      </p>
    </div>

  </main>

  <Footer current="/guides" />
</Base>
